      "id": "word-adicción--addictiveness",
      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "adicción",
      "answerEn": "addiction; addictive pull or quality",
      "noteEn": "Adicción usually names an addiction or dependence. It can also point to the quality that makes an activity very hard to stop, which English can call “addictiveness.”",
      "example": { "es": "El juego puede causar adicción.", "en": "The game can cause addiction." },
      "tags": ["word", "habit", "figurative quality", "B1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "word-de--property-source",
      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "de",
      "answerEn": "of; links a quality or effect to what has or causes it",
      "noteEn": "De can connect a quality, feature, or effect to the thing it comes from. English usually keeps “of” or uses a possessive form.",
      "example": { "es": "Me sorprende la fuerza de este viento.", "en": "This wind's force surprises me." },
      "tags": ["word", "preposition", "quality", "source", "A2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "word-del--superlative-group",
      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "del",
      "answerEn": "in the; introduces the group used for a ‘most’ or ‘least’ comparison",
      "noteEn": "Del combines de and el. After a description with más or menos that picks out an extreme, it can introduce the larger group being compared. Natural English often uses ‘in the’ rather than translating de literally as ‘of.’",
      "example": { "es": "Es el edificio más alto del barrio.", "en": "It is the tallest building in the neighborhood." },
      "tags": ["word", "contraction", "superlative", "comparison group", "A2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "word-flash--adobe-platform",
      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "flash",
      "answerEn": "Flash; using Adobe Flash technology",
      "noteEn": "Flash is the unchanged name of an older multimedia platform. In a phrase such as juegos Flash, it identifies the technology used to make or run the games.",
      "example": { "es": "El museo conserva una animación Flash.", "en": "The museum preserves a Flash animation." },
      "tags": ["word", "technology", "proper name", "web"]
    },
    {
      "id": "word-navegador--web-browser",
      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "navegador",
      "answerEn": "web browser",
      "noteEn": "Navegador can describe a navigator, but in computing it commonly means a web browser: the program used to open websites.",
      "example": { "es": "Abre el enlace en el navegador.", "en": "Open the link in the web browser." },
      "tags": ["word", "technology", "internet", "A2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "concept-flash-browser-games",
      "kind": "concept",
      "promptEs": "juegos Flash del navegador",
      "questionEn": "What were Flash browser games?",
      "answerEn": "They were games made with Adobe Flash that ran inside a web browser, usually through a small browser add-on called a plug-in.",
      "noteEn": "Flash supported animation, sound, and interaction, so it became a common platform for quick web games before modern browser technologies replaced it. Adobe ended support for Flash Player in 2020.",
      "example": { "es": "Muchos juegos Flash se abrían desde una página web.", "en": "Many Flash games opened from a web page." },
      "tags": ["concept", "Flash", "browser games", "internet history"]
    }
